     to contain; mmkkffss reads this file to build the file system.
     In the second, _n is the size of the file system in blocks,
     and mmkkffss constructs an empty file system of that size (hol-
     ding nothing but a root directory) using values taken from
     the option letters below, in place of a prototype file; a
     _p_r_o_t_o that is entirely digits selects this form, anything
     else selects the first form.  If any of the option letters
     are given together with a real _p_r_o_t_o file, they are super-
     fluous and mmkkffss warns and ignores them.

